    {
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "text": "## Problem\n\nLong-form technical and professional documents are difficult to use when notes stay disconnected from source evidence.",
      "heading_path": [
        "Retrieval Notes",
        "Problem"
      ],
      "content_hash": "7af2fb6f8dcc3d1fd31c5061072e3150109c95d74c1f7d834b9538886f484274",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6
    },
    {
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "text": "## Method\n\nThe workspace normalises input text, preserves headings, creates deterministic chunks, and stores provenance metadata for each document version.",
      "heading_path": [
        "Retrieval Notes",
        "Method"
      ],
      "content_hash": "867436d2322ba8323c18f453e81cd44c572d0906b34f3ca207a4f7b2a5e7c8bf",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 10
    },
    {
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "text": "## Evaluation\n\nThe first milestone checks stable normalisation, heading-aware chunking, content hashes, and JSON export. Later milestones add PostgreSQL storage, pgvector embeddings, hybrid retrieval, source-cited generation, and evaluation metrics.",
      "heading_path": [
        "Retrieval Notes",
        "Evaluation"
      ],
